# Source location: https://github.com/MelkhiorVintageComputing/RD68041
#
# make qvirt-linux FPU=0 (the MC68LC040): linux.mask's lines, and the one
# floating-point line the reference cannot give (doc/qvirt.md). QEMU's m68040
# has no MC68LC040 mode: with the bootinfo's FPU record cleared the kernel
# believes it has no FPU, but QEMU executes the FP instructions itself. On the
# core they take the F-line trap to the kernel's FPU emulation, which has no
# FATAN: /init's `awk float:` (atan2) gets the emulation's warning and value,
# exactly as on rd-virt's UAE040 with no FPU (M13's lockstep console). The
# command set's own FP line (commands-lc.script) is arithmetic the emulation
# does have, and is compared.
^Unpacking initramfs
goldfish_timer$
^awk float: 
^You just hit an unimplemented fpu instruction \(f[a-z]+$
^\)$
^Please report this to \.\.\.\.$
